      "description": "The user is projected onto the elderly man (VisualMaterial entity) because he is pointing directly at the viewer, creating a direct deictic relationship. The text 'it's funny because he's fat!' further reinforces this projection by framing the viewer's perspective as the one who finds the man's appearance humorous, making the user the implied subject of the joke. The pointing gesture and the accusatory tone of the text create a sense of direct address, where the user is positioned as the recipient of the humor or the target of the judgment.",
